              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Medical Marijuana argued that Horn\u2019s lost wages are merely \u201cdamages\u201d that derive from a personal injury and therefore are not recoverable under civil RICO."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Medical Marijuana",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f0ea5f7f316e00ac2150526cfc81dc97a3faeb3a5ef26b387754313ff90077c3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f0ea5f7f316e-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 32,
                "start": 32
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Medical Marijuana, medical Marijuana conceded that some harms to business or property are actionable under civil RICO, but asserted that not all economic harms, such as certain lost wages, should be treated as injuries to business or property."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Medical Marijuana",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "f0ea5f7f316e00ac2150526cfc81dc97a3faeb3a5ef26b387754313ff90077c3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-f0ea5f7f316e-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 33,
                "start": 33
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Medical Marijuana maintained that a plaintiff can bring a civil RICO suit only if a legally protected right in his business or property is invaded."
        }
      ],
